      <div type="clause" n="39">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 39</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXIII.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.7"/> Gif hwa fare unáliefed<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.8"/> fram his hlaforde oððe on oðre scire hine bestele, ⁊ hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.9"/> mon geahsige, fare þær he ær wæs ⁊ geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.10"/> his hlaforde LX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXXIII. Gif hwa fare unalyfed from<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.1-2"/> his hlaforde oððe on oðre scire hine bestele, ⁊ hine mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.1-2"/> geaxie, fare þær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.4-2"/> he wæs<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.5"/> ær ond<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.1-2"/> gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.3-2"/> his hlaforde LX scll'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="106" ed="#liebermann"/>Be unalyfedu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> fare fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> his laforde. Gyf hwá fare unalyfede fra<hi rend="italic">m</hi> his laforde oððe on oðre scire hine bestele, ⁊ hine man geacsige, fare ðær he ær wæs ⁊ gylde his laforde syxtig scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="39" corresp="#wit-q"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.star2"/><pb n="107" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis discedat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.1"/> a domino suo sine licentia uel<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.2"/> in alium comitatum se furetur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.3"/>, et (deinceps<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_39.lnote.oe.4"/>) inueniatur postea, redeat illuc, ubi antea fuit, et emendet domino suo LX sol.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="48" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be unalyfedum fare fram his laforde.] Gif hwa fare unáliefed fram his hlaforde<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_39.attnote.fn.10"/> oððe on oðre scire hine bestele, ⁊ hine mon geahsige<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Ine_39.attnote.fn.11"/>, fare þær he ær wæs ⁊ geselle<ptr type="editorNote" n="12" target="#Ine_39.attnote.fn.12"/> his hlaforde<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Ine_39.attnote.fn.10-2"/> LX scill.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="40" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="404" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>[{LXXXIII}] Gif hwa fare unáliefed fram his hlaforde oððe on oðre scire hine bestele, ⁊ hine mon geahsige, fare þær he ær wæs ⁊ geselle his hlaforde LX sciƚƚ.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="107" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn jemand von seinem Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_39.lnote.de.1"/> ohne Erlaubniss fortzieht oder sich in einen anderen Amtsbezirk<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_39.lnote.de.2"/> fortstiehlt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_39.lnote.de.3"/>, und man ihn erkundet, so ziehe er [dorthin zurück<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_39.lnote.de.4"/>], wo er früher war, und gebe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_39.lnote.de.5"/> seinem Herrn 60<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_39.lnote.de.6"/> Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone goes away from his lord without permission or steals away into another district, and he is discovered, let him go [back] to where he was before and give his lord 60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="49" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone moves away without permission from his lord and steals into another district<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_39.attnote.n.1"/>, if he is discovered he shall return to where he was before, and give his lord 60 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="404" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone goes away from his lord without permission, or steals into another “shire”,<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_39.whinote.n.4"/> and is discovered there, he is to return to where he was before and pay 60 shillings to his lord.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="405" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone moves away from his lord without permission or steals away into another shire, and he is found, let him return to where he was before and let him pay his lord 60 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:App-AGu_4">App AGu 4</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="274"><label>modifies</label> <ref target="clause:Af_37">Af 37</ref> <quote>Alfred's law modified one of Ine where the word used had been scir (n. 35: Af 37, cf. Ine 39)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="193"><label>based on</label> <ref target="clause:Af_37">Af 37–37.2</ref> <quote>Alfred's law is clearly based on Ine's, yet Alfred has to find another word, boldgetal, for Ine's scir</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="335"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Af_37">Af 37</ref> <quote>Compare Ine §40.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="337"><label>contrast</label> <ref target="clause:Af_37-1">Af 37.1</ref> <quote>Ine §40 requires that the man himself, not the lord, pay the fine: 60 shillings to his first lord.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="268"><label>follows (denied)</label> <ref target="clause:IIEw_7">II Ew 7</ref> <quote>nor is it really the case, as suggested in Gesetze III, p. 39 (36), that II Ew 7 followed Ine 39</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">App. ad Aelfr. Guthr. foedus</hi> (<hi rend="italic">s. o. S.</hi> 93*) 4: Si quis recedat a domino suo¹ sine² licentia uel in aliam³ schiram se subducat et inquiratur⁴, <hi rend="spaced">redeat</hi> ubi⁵ prius fuit⁶ et <hi rend="spaced">emendet</hi> domino suo LX sol.<lb type="paragraph"/>1) <hi rend="italic">fehlt T</hi> 2) preter licenciam <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi> 3) alium comitatum <hi rend="italic">TMHkBr</hi> 4) ubi sit <hi rend="italic">fügt zu TMHkBr</hi> 5) ut <hi rend="italic">K Or</hi> 6) sit <hi rend="italic">HkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">App. ad Aelfr. Guthr. foedus</hi> (see above p. 93*) 4: Si quis recedat a domino suo¹ sine² licentia uel in aliam³ schiram se subducat et inquiratur⁴, <hi rend="italic">redeat</hi> ubi⁵ prius fuit⁶ et <hi rend="italic">emendet</hi> domino suo LX sol.<lb type="paragraph"/>1) lacking in T 2) preter licenciam TMHkBr 3) alium comitatum TMHkBr 4) ubi sit added by TMHkBr 5) ut K Or 6) sit HkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-dit <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-dit Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">transferatur <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">transferatur Brti</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> inu. po. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> de. in. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only inu. po. Lond; only de. in. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in a</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">wæ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wæ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">III <hi rend="italic">wegen Raummangels unter</hi> LXXX <hi rend="italic">E</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">III below LXXX for lack of space E</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-leafed <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-leafed Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">m. h. geacsige <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">m. h. geacsige Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">106</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gylde his hlaford sixtig <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gylde his hlaford sixtig Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Freizügigkeit 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Freizügigkeit 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Es <hi rend="spaced">kann</hi> Grafschaft (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 3) gemeint sein, wie Q und Neuere verstehen; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 36, 1. Dann wäre die Erlaubnis auch des Ealdorman (<hi rend="italic">s.</hi> Af 37) schon hier erfordert. <hi rend="italic">Vgl.</hi> Herrensuche; Gefolge 8. 26. Laut des hohen Bussbetrags ist der Vassall kein armer Mann. Nicht zu denken ist an einen Gebur auf abhängigem Lande</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The shire (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 3) <hi rend="italic">may</hi> be meant, as Q and modern scholars understand it; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 36, 1. In that case the permission of the ealdorman too (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> Af 37) would already be required here. <hi rend="italic">Cf.</hi> Herrensuche; Gefolge 8. 26. Judging by the high amount of the compensation, the vassal is not a poor man. A gebur on dependent land is not to be thought of</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">= <hi rend="italic">hine forstalie,</hi> <hi rend="italic">o.</hi> 24; <hi rend="italic">se subducat</hi> Ap AGu 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">= <hi rend="italic">hine forstalie,</hi> <hi rend="italic">above</hi> 24; <hi rend="italic">se subducat</hi> Ap AGu 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">So richtig Q</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So Q, correctly</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘zahle’ B</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘let him pay’ B</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_39.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">75</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Bei Af 37⁴ hält der Staat das Gefolge noch schärfer im Zügel</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In Af 37⁴ the state keeps the retinue on an even tighter rein</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_39.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">48</biblScope></bibl><label>hlaforde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">laforde</hi>. B.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 10 is printed 2 times on the page (39, 39), with one footnote.</note></note>
