        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_39.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">189</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">See note 2 to cap. 8.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_39.whinote.n.4" n="4" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">404</biblScope></bibl><label>“shire”</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">In the early laws it is uncertain whether “shire” already bears its later definite meaning, or is used more generally of “jurisdiction”, or “district under one’s jurisdiction”.</seg></note>
